            <p>Herpes Zoster Ophthalmicus With Hutchinson Sign. Herpes Zoster, aka shingles, can involve the ophthalmic division of the trigeminal nerve, resulting in herpes zoster ophthalmicus. The Hutchinson sign, or&#x000a0;herpetic lesions in the nasal area, may precede this condition. <ext-link xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="https://dermnetnz.org/images">DermNet New Zealand</ext-link></p>
